# CMS staging auth gate (CFS) — the two CFS-template files MUST ship in
# the public mirror as generic placeholders (the operator substitutes the
# CFS-portal-issued versions at runbook time per docs/auth-gate.md).
# Pattern below: re-include the directory traversal, RE-EXCLUDE everything
# inside (so per-developer files like runtimeConfig.<user>.json stay
# excluded), then re-include only the two specific auth-gate files.
# Order matters: parent directories must be re-included before child
# files. See spec .kiro/specs/2026-06-01-cms-staging-auth-gate/spec.md.
!modules/cms_ui/source/frontend/public/
modules/cms_ui/source/frontend/public/*
!modules/cms_ui/source/frontend/public/error/
!modules/cms_ui/source/frontend/public/error/403.html
!modules/cms_ui/source/frontend/public/js/
!modules/cms_ui/source/frontend/public/js/cfs-handler.js

