# yarn.lock is a DEPENDENCY lockfile, not a runtime lock — it must be committed
# (~/.kiro/steering/virtual-environments.md: "Lock files in version control —
# always commit lock files"). The `*.lock` rule above lives under "Logs and
# Runtime Files" and was aimed at things like setuptools' vendor `.lock` and PID
# locks; it caught yarn.lock as collateral, so no dependency lockfile was tracked
# at all. CI then failed on `yarn install --immutable` with YN0028 "the lockfile
# would have been CREATED by this install" — a clean checkout had none.
# See issues/2026-09-24-frontend-yarn-lock-never-tracked/.
!modules/cms_ui/source/frontend/yarn.lock
