# Spec 2026-05-28-cms-staging-502-and-monitor-hardening: hardened ios-monitor.py
# carries the privacy redaction (_redact), per-session signature dedup
# (_signature + seen_signatures), and benign-noise suppression (BENIGN_PATTERNS).
# MUST ship to the team — without git tracking the redaction control exists only
# on one engineer's local machine. Tracked exception to the scripts/ exclude.
!scripts/ios-monitor.py
# Spec 2026-09-15-cms-cs-campaign-ownership Task 7.1: FWELogViewer parity drift-guard.
# `.github/workflows/lint.yml`'s `renderer-parity` job invokes this file by path, so
# it MUST be tracked — a guard that is not checked out is not a guard. It asserts the
# cms_ui and connected_services_ui copies of FWELogViewer.tsx stay byte-identical
# (bar one allowlisted import line).
#
# NOTE the negation below does NOT make `git add` work: line 635's `scripts` excludes
# the DIRECTORY, and git will not consider a file inside an excluded directory, so a
# per-file negation cannot re-include it. `git add -f` is required. The negation is
# retained only to document intent, consistent with `!scripts/rename-oem1-protos.py`
# and `!scripts/ios-monitor.py` above, which are decorative for the same reason.
# Re-including properly needs the ordered three-line form used for
# `clients/ios/scripts/` (re-include dir, re-exclude contents, re-include the file) —
# not done here because `/scripts/*` would shadow the later `!scripts/lib/*`
# negations the publish toolkit depends on. Tracked as
# issues/2026-09-15-scripts-gitignore-negations-are-decorative/.
!scripts/verify_cs_log_viewer_parity.py
# OEM1 A2.3: cleansed vendor protos (committed under services/connectors/oem1/proto/;
# *.proto is otherwise excluded)
!services/connectors/oem1/proto/**/*.proto
!services/connectors/oem1/proto/**
DecoderManifest.bin
# WS1 (spec 2026-06-18-cms-fwe-decoder-manifest-bucket-resolution): the stack-managed
# copy under deployment/fwe-config/ IS version-controlled — it is the BucketDeployment
# source uploaded into the Flink jar bucket the CampaignSyncProcessor reads. Only the
# generator's transient ./DecoderManifest.bin remains ignored. Without this negation a
# clean checkout deploys an empty fwe-config/ → empty manifest → FWE telemetry outage.
!deployment/fwe-config/DecoderManifest.bin

